Text: M-BERT’s performance, on the other hand, is ﬂat for a wide range of overlaps, and even for language pairs with almost no lexical overlap, scores vary between 40% and 70%, showing that M-BERT’s pretraining on multiple languages has enabled a representational capacity deeper than simple vocabulary memorization.5 To further verify that EN-BERT’s inability to generalize is due to its lack of a multilingual rep- resentation and not an inability of its English- speciﬁc word piece vocabulary to represent data in other languages, we evaluate on non-cross-lingual NER and see that it performs comparably to a pre- vious state of the art model (see Table 3).

